Project-section guidance:
- Prioritize technically substantial, complex, user-facing, production-like,
  or genuine open-source work over tutorial-grade projects.
- Keep every project's source link and stack exactly grounded in the input.
- Use bullets to show implementation depth, testing, integration, contribution,
  constraints, or outcomes rather than merely naming the project or tools.
- Preserve distinctive project context while translating internal terminology
  into language an external reader can understand.
